 ## Background
-The method was introduced in the paper "Vanishing Point Aided Hash-Frequency Encoding for Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) from Sparse 360° Input" [S1]. It builds on Instant-NGP's hash encoding  and NeurVPS for vanishing point estimation . The work addresses the limitations of existing methods for view synthesis from sparse inputs, which may require costly pre-training or additional regularization steps [S1]. It incorporates scene-encoding alignment by estimating vanishing points and modifying the input encoding scheme to ensure alignment with scene geometry [S1].
